# Schemas (`packages/schemas`)

Runtime contracts live here, not in ad-hoc types in web or api. Zod 4.4.3
(same major as both apps). Export the schema and `z.infer` the type.

```ts
// ✅
export const healthResponseSchema = z.object({
  status: z.enum(["ok", "degraded", "error"]),
  api: serviceStatusSchema,
  database: serviceStatusSchema,
});
export type HealthResponse = z.infer<typeof healthResponseSchema>;

// ❌
export interface HealthResponse { status: string }
```

- Re-export public schemas and types from `src/index.ts`.
- Web and API both `parse()` the same schema. Do not duplicate shapes.
- `signUpSchema` and `signInSchema` (`src/auth.ts`) validate client-side input
  only (password ≥ 8). Better Auth validates the server — these are NOT
  applied to `/api/auth/*`.
- Workspace/project GET contracts live in `src/workspace.ts`
  (`workspaceListResponseSchema`, `projectSchema`, `projectIdParamSchema`,
  `workspacesQuerySchema`).   Board/move contracts live in `src/board.ts`.
  Comment contracts live in `src/comment.ts` (`commentSchema` with
  `authorName`, `createCommentBodySchema`, `commentListResponseSchema`).
  `@Nombre` tokens: `extractMentionNames` in `src/mention.ts` (unique,
  no member resolution). Notification inbox contracts live in
  `src/notification.ts` (`notificationSchema` with `actorName`,
  `taskTitle`, `bodyPreview`, nullable `readAt`).
  Board announcement events live in `src/events.ts` (`boardEventSchema`,
  discriminated on `type`: task.created / updated / deleted / moved /
  comment.created; `applyBoardEvent` patches a `Board` snapshot and is a
  no-op for comments; `boardEventToastMessage` is the in-app sonner copy).
  HTTP remains the write path.
  The API parses responses with the same schemas.
  `workspaceId` in JSON is data, not permission.
-   Tests: `import { describe, expect, it } from "vite-plus/test"`. Cover a
  valid parse and a reject path (see `src/health.test.ts`, `src/auth.test.ts`,
  `src/workspace.test.ts`, `src/board.test.ts`, `src/events.test.ts`,
  `src/comment.test.ts`, `src/mention.test.ts`,
  `src/notification.test.ts`).
